# TCP options sitting exactly on their length bounds:
#   SACK with length==2 satisfies `length >= 2` with equality and yields a zero-byte
#   subrange, so the inner [..]SackBlock loop runs zero times.
#   The `..` default arm with length==2 yields data :[0]u8, a zero-length array.
01 bb # src port
c0 a8 # dst port
00 00 00 01 # seq number
00 00 00 00 # ack number
6 # data offset (6*4 = 24 -> 4 bytes of options)
0 # reserved
10 # flags ACK=true
00 1c # window size
00 00 # check sum
00 00 # urgent pointer
# Options (4 bytes)
05 # SACK
02 # len=2 -> subrange of 0 bytes, zero SackBlocks
1e # MPTCP -> `..` default arm
02 # len=2 -> data :[0]u8
# no payload
